The '''TIE/wi interceptor''', also referred to as the '''TIE whisper''' or simply the '''whisper''', was a [[First Order]] [[TIE series|TIE fighter series]] [[interceptor]] used during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[Resistance]]. During the war, [[Supreme Leader]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] utilised his [[Kylo Ren's TIE whisper|modified TIE whisper]] in the [[search for Exegol]] and to confront [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] on the planet [[Pasaana]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:EnhancedJammingSuite-SWZ87.png|thumb|300px|left|TIE whispers were equipped with enhanced sensor jamming which gave them an advantage in battle.]]
The TIE/wi interceptor was a [[starfighter]] which was brought up to the exact specification of [[Supreme Leader]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] of the [[First Order]]. As such, it had increased speed, range, and more firepower than a standard model. It was manufactured by [[Sienar-Jaemus Fleet Systems]] and like other [[starship]]s of the [[TIE series|TIE fighter series]], had a [[twin ion engine]] capable of reaching [[Sublight engine|sublight]] speeds of 140 [[Megalight per hour|MGLT]],<ref name="SWEOSAOV SE" /> and its wings were [[solar collector]]s, which were similar in appearance to Ren's previous ship, the [[TIE/vn space superiority fighter]]. It had four [[laser cannon]]s at the tip of each wing, five heavy cannons between the two main solar collectors on each wing, and a heavy weapons turret with mag-pulses and heavy lasers. In addition, it had a round [[cockpit]] that featured [[Color|red]] designs and an antenna at the rear. The TIE whisper was also equipped with [[sensor]]-confusing technology,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> such as its [[enhanced jamming suite]],<ref name="Enhanced Jamming">{{FFGXW2|set=Fury of the First Order Squadron Pack|cardname=Enhanced Jamming Suite}}</ref> that allowed for a degree of stealth.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The vessel was also equipped with a Class 1 [[hyperdrive]].<ref name="SWEOSAOV SE" />

==History==
The TIE whisper entered service during the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the First Order and the [[Resistance]], with a [[Kylo Ren's TIE whisper|modified one]] piloted by Ren, replacing his [[TIE/vn space superiority fighter]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref> The [[First Order TIE fighter pilot|First Order TIE Fighter Pilot]] "[["Wrath"|Wrath]]" flew a TIE whisper in battle against Resistance forces, including [[T-70 X-wing starfighter]]s.<ref name="Wrath Card">{{FFGXW2|set=Fury of the First Order Squadron Pack|cardname="Wrath"}}</ref> Pilot "[["Nightfall"|Nightfall]]," a veteran of<ref name="Nightfall">{{FFGXW2|set=Fury of the First Order Squadron Pack|cardname="Nightfall"}}</ref> the elite<ref name="Black Spire">''[[Galaxy's Edge: Black Spire]]''</ref> 709th Legion, flew a TIE whisper and used the craft to chase after a [[RZ-2 A-wing interceptor]] over a rocky area.<ref name="Nightfall" /> The pilot "[["Whirlwind"|Whirlwind]]" flew a whisper in battle against [[BTA-NR2 Y-wing starfighter]]s.<ref name="Whirlwind">{{FFGXW2|set=Fury of the First Order Squadron Pack|cardname="Whirlwind"}}</ref> One TIE/wi was once involved in a battle against enemy [[X-wing starfighter]]s and [[CR-series|Alderaanian crusiers]] alongside a formation of other TIE ships. In the battle, the TIE whisper, all while firing two [[missile]]s, utilized its enhanced hamming suit and flew past an explosion that rippled across one of the enemy [[cruiser]]s.<ref name="Enhanced Jamming" />

[[File:TIEwhisper-TROS.png|thumb|right|300px|Kylo Ren in his TIE whisper on Pasaana]]
Ren used his TIE whisper to travel to [[Exegol]] where he confronted [[Darth Sidious]], who revealed the [[Sith Eternal]]'s fleet of [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyers]], the [[Final Order]], and ordered him to kill [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] and end the Jedi. Ren later used his TIE to confront the [[Jedi]] Rey on the [[desert]] [[Planet|world]] [[Pasaana]], during which she jumped over his ship and sliced off one of its wings, causing it to crash. Ren flew another TIE of the same model to [[Kef Bir]], where he again confronted Rey in a lightsaber duel. Defeating and wounding him, Rey took the TIE and flew it to [[Ahch-To]], where she burned it, pledging that she would follow the path of [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] and exile herself to the island. However, Skywalker's [[Force spirit]] confronted her and convinced her to continue the fight. Rey then took the wayfinder from the wreckage and departed the planet in Luke's [[Red Five (T-65B X-wing starfighter)|old]] [[X-wing starfighter]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Behind the scenes==
The TIE whisper appears in [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] and was first seen during the official teaser for the film.<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|adzYW5DZoWs|Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker &ndash; Teaser|sw_url=video/star-wars-episode-ix-teaser}}</ref> It was first identified in ''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The reference book ''[[Star Wars Origami 2: 34 More Projects from a Galaxy Far, Far Away....]]'' mistakenly identified the TIE whisper as an Imperial Era starfighter.<ref name="Origami">''[[Star Wars Origami 2: 34 More Projects from a Galaxy Far, Far Away....]]''</ref>

